<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Dar al Kuti</h1><p class="st-meta">1830 CE – 1911 CE (approx.) · capital Ndele</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Muslim slave-raiding sultanate on the northern edge of the Central African forest, ruled from Ndele by the warlord al-Sanusi.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Dar al Kuti arose in the 19th century as a frontier province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai</a>, where Muslim traders and settlers from Dar Runga established themselves among the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-banda">Banda</a> and Kara peoples south of the Chari basin. Its rulers were tributaries of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The economy depended on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slave-raiding">slave raiding</a> into the populous lands to the south and on trading captives and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> north to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-sanusi-of-dar-al-kuti">Muhammad al-Sanusi</a>, who took power in 1890 with the backing of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rabih-az-zubayrs-state">Rabih az-Zubayr</a>, built a fortified capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndele">Ndele</a> from 1896, with mosques, granaries and a firearm-equipped army, and carried out large raids each dry season.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Al-Sanusi accepted a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1897, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> turned against him and he was killed in 1911. The sultanate was absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ubangi-shari">Ubangi-Shari</a>, and its raids left much of the region depopulated.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sultanate-of-dar-al-kuti.jpg" alt="Sultanate of Dar al Kuti" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: CromwellTheTuco · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dar_Al_Kuti_Sultanate_Banner.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1830 CE – 1911 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ndele</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad al-Kuti, Muhammad al-Sanusi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Banda, Runga</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/central-african-republic">Central African Republic</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dar al Kuti, Senoussi's sultanate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1870&amp;focus=sultanate-of-dar-al-kuti" aria-label="Sultanate of Dar al Kuti on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5259 1916 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sultanate of Dar al Kuti lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5382 1985h0M5515 2270h0M5571 1919h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5579 2172h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5579 2172h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Central African Republic. <a href="/atlas?year=1870&amp;focus=sultanate-of-dar-al-kuti">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

